# NestedText v3 - xhtml/ per-folder DETAIL pass (measured 2026-09-16)
# Source: cc-resources/.dtd-file-examples/xhtml/ - 373 files, 2.1 MB
# Supersedes nothing; xhtml.nt is the folder index, this is the detail it deferred.
# Ordinal: duo, Greek per the 10.0.0 rule that every created file is numbered.
# Fifth of the F18-rest detail passes.

three-drivers:
    > xhtml1-strict.dtd, xhtml1-transitional.dtd, xhtml1-frameset.dtd: one
    > vocabulary in three conformance profiles, strict inside transitional
    > inside frameset by inclusion. Conformance as subtraction: each driver
    > names what it refuses, never what it adds.

second-grammars:
    > relaxng 40 files beside the dtd/ drivers; nvdl 3 files dispatching
    > between them. The folder carries its own multi-schema publishing
    > beside DocBook's: DTD for validation, RELAX NG for extension, NVDL
    > for choosing per namespace.

reverse-transform:
    > html2dita 16 files: the only reverse pipeline in the corpus, HTML
    > back into DITA topic types. Every other transform in every other
    > folder runs forward from authoring to output; this one proves the
    > vocabulary round-trips, which is what a reconstituted cache claims.

epub3-profile:
    > xhtml5-(epub3)/ carries mod/html5, mod/mathml, mod/security and
    > mod/svg11 beside dict, edupub and idx: a delivery profile composed
    > of modules, the same composition the installer performs over
    > RUNTIME entries.

release-binding:
    > Stream 9 (corpus convergence): the strict-inside-transitional
    > inclusion is the subset pattern for converging corpora without
    > copying them. Stream 17 (audit legs): html2dita is the precedent
    > for legs that read the built tree back into the source shape.
